 "_boundary_note": "PTF-TAMPA-FL-HARDENED-V2-SOURCE-READY-001. Tampa, St. Petersburg and Clearwater/the Gulf beaches are treated as ONE Tampa Bay market, not three: they sit inside a single Census-defined Tampa-St. Petersburg-Clearwater MSA, are joined by causeway/interstate connectivity (Howard Frankland, Courtney Campbell, Gandy, Sunshine Skyway), and share the 'Tampa Bay' travel identity even where Visit Tampa Bay and Visit St. Pete-Clearwater run separate CVBs. That separate-CVB / separate-county reality is preserved as CORRIDOR-level distinction (St. Petersburg and Clearwater/the Gulf beaches are named CORRIDOR tiers, never folded anonymously into generic Tampa corridors), not as three markets. A multi-core market: nine CORE corridors (Downtown Tampa/Riverwalk, Ybor City, Westshore/TPA Airport, Rocky Point, Raymond James Stadium/Himes-Dale Mabry, Busch Gardens/USF, Temple Terrace, Brandon, East Tampa/I-75), eight CORRIDOR (Downtown St. Petersburg, St. Petersburg, Clearwater, Clearwater Beach, St. Pete Beach, Treasure Island, Madeira Beach/Redington/Indian Rocks Beach, Largo) and six FRINGE (Wesley Chapel/New Tampa, South Hillsborough/Riverview/Apollo Beach/Ruskin, Plant City, Tarpon Springs/Dunedin, mid-Pinellas/Seminole/Pinellas Park/Gulfport, Safety Harbor/Oldsmar/Palm Harbor). Standalone-market optionality is preserved for a future 'Pinellas beaches' or 'st-petersburg-fl' split if traveler behavior later diverges further; this build does not force that split. Sarasota/Bradenton, Anna Maria Island, Lakeland and Spring Hill/Brooksville are OBSERVED and REFUSED, preserved for possible future standalone markets. Orlando is its own separate, already-built market and is OUTSIDE by definition (no Orlando-oriented inventory is admitted here).",
